{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) at 52.7% acc, modestly above RNA-only (48.5%) and far above image-only (20.8%). All three completed experiments use singleprofile, leaving the multiprofile dimension entirely unexplored. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) improve the multimodal model over the single-profile baseline, while keeping the same RNA encoder, image encoder, and concat fusion? Why this experiment: config_018 is the minimal logical extension of the current best into the untested multiprofile space—it changes only the profile setting and adds the necessary avgpool aggregation. This balances exploitation (staying in the proven multimodal/pca/resnet50/concat regime) with exploration of a potentially high-impact architectural choice. A positive result directly upgrades our best configuration; a negative result efficiently rules out multiprofile in the multimodal setting and redirects budget toward other dimensions (fusion strategy, image encoder, RNA encoder)."
}

